Package: hd-backup
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), python3, python3-colorama, python3-tabulate, systemd, hd-config, zfsutils-linux, zstd, libvirt-clients, udev
Recommends: mbuffer, mt-st
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: HyprDebian backup tools
 hd-backup writes backups of filesets as tarballs to hard drives or LTO tape,
 and keeps track of what is on which carrier in a SQLite database. On tape,
 blockwrite writes the stream in fixed blocks of 4 MiB. hd-backup-prep turns
 a whole drive into an encrypted ZFS pool to hold the backups, and
 hd-backup-load and hd-backup-unload connect and disconnect it.
 .
 hd-backup-vm backs up a virtual machine of libvirt whose disks are ZFS
 volumes, with full and then incremental ZFS streams, and hd-restore-vm
 restores it. hd-backup-vms backs up every VM in the key hd-backup of
 /etc/hyprdebian/config.json; hd-backup-vms.timer runs it every night at
 3:30. The package does not enable the timer.
